 "label": "Colour Grade",
 "category": "Colour Correction",
 "tags": ["look"],
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "One place to grade a shot, in the order a colourist works. Basic correction balances it: temperature and tint, exposure in stops, contrast around mid grey, highlights, shadows, whites and blacks, saturation and a vibrance that spares skin. Creative gives it a look: faded film, sharpening and a split tone for the shadows and highlights. Curves shape brightness and each channel, and hue against saturation, hue and brightness. The three colour wheels push the shadows, midtones and highlights towards a colour and lift or lower each; drag the dots in the wheels above the rows. HSL secondary picks one colour range, such as skin or sky, and grades only that. Vignette darkens or brightens the edges.",
